(window.FREE_Q = window.FREE_Q || {})["ibps-clerk"] = {"qs": [["Reasoning Ability", "Which letter of the English alphabet is 5th to the left of the 16th letter from the left end?", ["K", "U", "L", "J"], 0, "The 16th letter from the left is P. Moving 5 places to its left gives the 11th letter, K. Moving to the right instead would give U."], ["English Language", "Choose the word that best fills the blank.\nThe loan amount will be credited ________ your savings account within two working days.", ["at", "of", "by", "to"], 3, "Money is credited to an account, so 'to' is the correct preposition. 'At', 'of' and 'by' do not combine with 'credited' to show the destination of the money."], ["Numerical Ability", "A can complete a piece of work in 20 days and B in 30 days. A works alone for 10 days and then leaves. In how many days will B finish the remaining work?", ["12 days", "18 days", "15 days", "10 days"], 2, "In 10 days A completes 10/20 = half the work. B does 1/30 per day, so the remaining half takes 30 × 1/2 = 15 days."], ["Reasoning Ability", "Neha's mother is the sister of Ravi's father. How is Ravi related to Neha?", ["Brother", "Cousin", "Nephew", "Uncle"], 1, "Neha's mother and Ravi's father are siblings. Children of siblings are cousins, so Ravi is Neha's cousin. He cannot be her brother because they have different parents."], ["Numerical Ability", "One card is drawn at random from a well-shuffled pack of 52 cards. What is the probability that it is a king or a heart?", ["17/52", "1/4", "5/13", "4/13"], 3, "There are 13 hearts and 4 kings, but the king of hearts is counted twice. Favourable cards = 13 + 4 − 1 = 16, so P = 16/52 = 4/13. Not subtracting the overlap gives 17/52."], ["English Language", "Identify the part of the sentence that contains an error.\nAll the customers were (A) / asked to stand (B) / in a queue and (C) / wait for there turn. (D)", ["(A)", "(B)", "(C)", "(D)"], 3, "'There' is an adverb of place; the possessive pronoun needed here is 'their', as in 'wait for their turn'. So part (D) contains the error."], ["English Language", "Choose the one word for: 'A list of items to be discussed at a meeting'.", ["Minutes", "Memo", "Agenda", "Notice"], 2, "An agenda lists the topics to be taken up at a meeting. Minutes are the written record of what was discussed afterwards, a common confusion, while a memo or notice is a general communication."], ["Reasoning Ability", "Find the wrong number in the series:\n2, 5, 11, 23, 48, 95", ["23", "11", "48", "95"], 2, "Each term is double the previous term plus 1: 2, 5, 11, 23, 47, 95. So 48 should be 47. Note that 95 = 47 × 2 + 1, which confirms 48 is the wrong term."], ["English Language", "Choose the option that best replaces the part in capitals. If no change is needed, choose 'No improvement required'.\nIf it rains tomorrow, we WILL STAYED at home.", ["will stay", "would stayed", "will staying", "No improvement required"], 0, "After the modal 'will', the base form of the verb is used: 'will stay'. In a first conditional, the if-clause takes simple present (rains) and the main clause takes 'will' + base verb."], ["Reasoning Ability", "Six boxes P, Q, R, S, T and U are placed one above another.\n• U is at the bottom.\n• Only two boxes are placed between U and Q.\n• Q is immediately above T.\n• P is immediately above Q.\n• R is placed somewhere above S.\nWhich box is at the top?", ["P", "S", "Q", "R"], 3, "U is 1st from bottom, so Q is 4th and T 3rd. P is 5th. R and S fill positions 2 and 6, and R must be above S, so R is on top (6th) and S is 2nd."], ["English Language", "Read the passage and answer the question.\nSunita, a farmer near Nashik, used to borrow from a local moneylender who charged very high interest. After she joined a self-help group, she could take small loans at a much lower rate and repay them in easy instalments. Within two years she bought a water pump and her onion yield nearly doubled.\nAs used in the passage, the word 'yield' most nearly means:", ["Surrender", "Profit share", "Output", "Interest"], 2, "In farming, 'yield' means the amount of crop produced, that is the output. 'Surrender' is another meaning of the verb 'yield', but it does not fit the context of onion harvests."], ["Reasoning Ability", "Find the odd one out:\n121, 169, 225, 289, 323", ["225", "169", "289", "323"], 3, "121, 169, 225 and 289 are squares of 11, 13, 15 and 17. 323 is not a perfect square (it is 17 × 19), so it is the odd one out."], ["Numerical Ability", "What will come in place of the question mark (?) in the series?\n2, 6, 15, 31, 56, ?", ["88", "87", "92", "94"], 2, "The differences are 4, 9, 16, 25, which are squares of 2, 3, 4, 5. The next difference is 6² = 36, so the missing term is 56 + 36 = 92."], ["English Language", "Identify the part of the sentence that contains an error.\nMy brother and I (A) / goes to the bank (B) / every Saturday (C) / to deposit money. (D)", ["(A)", "(B)", "(C)", "(D)"], 1, "Two subjects joined by 'and' (My brother and I) take a plural verb. So 'goes' must be 'go'. The error lies in part (B); the other parts are correct."], ["Reasoning Ability", "Statements: All banks are buildings. No building is a tent.\nConclusions: I. No bank is a tent. II. Some buildings are banks.", ["Only conclusion I follows", "Only conclusion II follows", "Both I and II follow", "Neither I nor II follows"], 2, "Banks lie wholly inside buildings, and buildings share nothing with tents, so no bank can be a tent. Since all banks are buildings, some buildings are certainly banks. Both conclusions follow."], ["Numerical Ability", "An amount of ₹1,350 is divided among A, B and C in the ratio 2 : 3 : 4. What is C's share?", ["₹450", "₹600", "₹300", "₹540"], 1, "Total parts = 2 + 3 + 4 = 9, so one part is 1,350 ÷ 9 = ₹150. C gets 4 parts = ₹600. ₹450 is B's share and ₹300 is A's share."], ["Numerical Ability", "The area of a rectangular plot is 432 m² and its length is 24 m. What is the perimeter of the plot?", ["84 m", "72 m", "96 m", "80 m"], 0, "Breadth = 432 ÷ 24 = 18 m. Perimeter = 2 × (24 + 18) = 84 m. Remember to add length and breadth before doubling, not just to double one side."], ["Reasoning Ability", "In a class of 35 students, Arun ranks 8th from the top. What is his rank from the bottom?", ["27th", "28th", "29th", "26th"], 1, "Rank from bottom = total − rank from top + 1 = 35 − 8 + 1 = 28th. Forgetting to add 1 gives 27th, a common slip."], ["Numerical Ability", "The marked price of a ceiling fan is ₹2,000. The shopkeeper allows a 10% discount and still makes a 20% profit. What is the cost price of the fan?", ["₹1,600", "₹1,440", "₹1,550", "₹1,500"], 3, "Selling price = 90% of 2,000 = ₹1,800. This includes a 20% profit, so cost price = 1,800 ÷ 1.2 = ₹1,500. Taking 20% off ₹1,800 gives ₹1,440, a common error."], ["Reasoning Ability", "In the following question, the relationship between different elements is shown. Decide which conclusion(s) definitely hold true.\nGiven: R > S ≥ T ≥ U\nConclusions: I. R > U  II. S > U", ["Only conclusion I follows", "Only conclusion II follows", "Both I and II follow", "Neither I nor II follows"], 0, "R > S ≥ T ≥ U gives R > U because one strict sign is present, so I follows. Between S and U all signs are ≥, so S may equal U; II is not definite. Only I follows."], ["Reasoning Ability", "A is the brother of B. B is the daughter of C. D is the husband of C. How is A related to D?", ["Son", "Nephew", "Brother", "Grandson"], 0, "B is C's daughter, and A is B's brother, so A is C's son. D is C's husband, so D is A's father. Hence A is D's son."], ["Numerical Ability", "Find the roots of each quadratic below and decide how x relates to y.\nI. x² + 5x + 6 = 0\nII. y² + 7y + 12 = 0", ["x > y", "x ≥ y", "x ≤ y", "Relationship cannot be established"], 1, "I gives x = −2 or −3; II gives y = −3 or −4. Every x is greater than or equal to every y, and x = y = −3 is possible, so x ≥ y. Watch the signs with negative roots."], ["English Language", "Read the passage and answer the question.\nSunita, a farmer near Nashik, used to borrow from a local moneylender who charged very high interest. After she joined a self-help group, she could take small loans at a much lower rate and repay them in easy instalments. Within two years she bought a water pump and her onion yield nearly doubled.\nWhat helped Sunita get loans at a lower rate of interest?", ["Joining a self-help group", "Selling her onion crop early", "Borrowing from the moneylender", "Buying a new water pump"], 0, "The passage says that after she joined a self-help group she could take small loans at a much lower rate. The moneylender charged high interest, and the pump was bought later with the loan."], ["Reasoning Ability", "Five officers V, W, X, Y and Z visit a branch on different days from Monday to Friday.\n• X visits on Wednesday.\n• W visits on the day immediately after Y.\n• Z visits on a day before X.\n• V does not visit on Monday.\nWho visits on Monday?", ["V", "Y", "W", "Z"], 3, "Y–W must be Monday–Tuesday or Thursday–Friday. If Monday–Tuesday, Z has no day before Wednesday, so Y–W are Thursday–Friday. V cannot take Monday, so V is Tuesday and Z is Monday."], ["Numerical Ability", "The average age of 30 students in a class is 14 years. When the teacher's age is included, the average rises by 1 year. What is the teacher's age?", ["45 years", "44 years", "46 years", "40 years"], 0, "Total age of students = 30 × 14 = 420. With the teacher, total = 31 × 15 = 465. Teacher's age = 465 − 420 = 45 years."], ["Numerical Ability", "What will come in place of the question mark (?)\n45% of 640 + 15² − 18 × 7 = ?", ["387", "377", "397", "367"], 0, "45% of 640 = 288, 15² = 225 and 18 × 7 = 126. So 288 + 225 − 126 = 387. Follow BODMAS: finish percentage, square and product before adding and subtracting."], ["English Language", "Identify the part of the sentence that contains an error.\nThe news (A) / about the merger (B) / were announced (C) / yesterday morning. (D)", ["(A)", "(B)", "(C)", "(D)"], 2, "'News' looks plural but is an uncountable singular noun, so it takes 'was': 'The news was announced'. The error is in part (C)."], ["Numerical Ability", "The sum of the present ages of a mother and her daughter is 50 years. Five years ago, the mother was seven times as old as the daughter. What is the mother's present age?", ["35 years", "42 years", "38 years", "40 years"], 3, "Let the daughter be d; mother = 50 − d. Then 45 − d = 7(d − 5), so 8d = 80 and d = 10. Mother is 40 years old. Check: five years ago 35 = 7 × 5."], ["Numerical Ability", "A car covers a certain distance at 60 km/h in 5 hours. At what speed must it travel to cover the same distance in 4 hours?", ["70 km/h", "75 km/h", "80 km/h", "72 km/h"], 1, "Distance = 60 × 5 = 300 km. To cover 300 km in 4 hours, speed = 300 ÷ 4 = 75 km/h. Speed and time are inversely proportional for a fixed distance."], ["English Language", "Rearrange the sentences to form a meaningful paragraph.\nP: First, she took a withdrawal slip from the counter and filled it in.\nQ: Asha reached the bank at ten in the morning.\nR: After checking her signature, the cashier gave her the cash.\nS: Then she stood in the queue and handed the slip to the cashier.", ["QSPR", "PQSR", "QPSR", "QPRS"], 2, "Q opens with Asha arriving, P begins the process with 'First', S follows with 'Then', and R ends with the cashier paying her. The time words fix the order as QPSR."], ["Numerical Ability", "The number of savings accounts opened by a bank branch on five days of a week was:\nMonday – 45, Tuesday – 60, Wednesday – 38, Thursday – 52, Friday – 55\nWhat is the average number of accounts opened per day?", ["48", "52", "50", "54"], 2, "Total accounts = 45 + 60 + 38 + 52 + 55 = 250. Average = 250 ÷ 5 = 50 accounts per day. Add carefully before dividing; one slip in the total changes the answer."], ["English Language", "Choose the correct meaning of the idiom: 'To turn over a new leaf'.", ["To start reading a new book", "To plant trees in a new garden", "To move to a new house or city", "To change one's behaviour for the better"], 3, "'Turn over a new leaf' means to make a fresh start by improving one's conduct or habits. The literal readings about books, plants or houses are traps."], ["English Language", "Choose the word that best fills the blank.\nThe cashier counted the notes ________ before handing them over to the customer.", ["carefully", "careful", "care", "careless"], 0, "The blank describes how the cashier counted, so an adverb is needed: 'carefully'. 'Careful' is an adjective and 'care' is a noun; 'careless' is an adjective with the opposite sense."], ["English Language", "Read the passage and answer the question.\nSunita, a farmer near Nashik, used to borrow from a local moneylender who charged very high interest. After she joined a self-help group, she could take small loans at a much lower rate and repay them in easy instalments. Within two years she bought a water pump and her onion yield nearly doubled.\nWhich of the following best describes what the passage is mainly about?", ["Why moneylenders charge very high interest", "How onions are grown in Nashik district", "Why farmers should avoid all kinds of loans", "How cheaper credit improved a farmer's life"], 3, "The passage traces Sunita's move from costly moneylender loans to cheaper group loans and the resulting rise in her yield. Its focus is on how affordable credit improved her livelihood."], ["Reasoning Ability", "In a certain code, BANK is written as YZMP. How is CASH written in that code?", ["XZGS", "DBTI", "XAHS", "XZHS"], 3, "Each letter is replaced by its opposite letter in the alphabet (A↔Z, B↔Y, N↔M, K↔P). For CASH: C→X, A→Z, S→H, H→S, giving XZHS."], ["English Language", "Pick the antonym of EXPAND.", ["Contract", "Extend", "Enlarge", "Spread"], 0, "To expand is to become larger. 'Contract' means to become smaller, so it is the opposite. Extend, enlarge and spread are all close in meaning to expand."], ["English Language", "Select the word that means the same as GENUINE.", ["Fake", "Authentic", "Rude", "Fragile"], 1, "Genuine means real or truly what it is said to be, so 'authentic' is the synonym. 'Fake' is its antonym, and rude or fragile are unrelated in meaning."], ["English Language", "Choose the word that best fills the blank.\nPlease ________ the account-opening form in capital letters.", ["fall", "fill", "feel", "fell"], 1, "One fills (in) a form, so 'fill' is correct. 'Fall', 'feel' and 'fell' are similar-sounding words but make no sense with 'the account-opening form'."], ["Numerical Ability", "At simple interest, a sum of money amounts to ₹7,200 in 2 years and to ₹8,400 in 4 years. What is the rate of interest per annum?", ["12%", "8%", "10%", "15%"], 2, "The extra ₹1,200 over 2 years means SI of ₹600 per year. Principal = 7,200 − 2 × 600 = ₹6,000. Rate = 600 ÷ 6,000 × 100 = 10% per annum."], ["Numerical Ability", "A student scored 36% marks and failed by 18 marks. If the pass mark is 45%, what are the maximum marks of the exam?", ["200", "180", "250", "225"], 0, "The gap between the pass mark and the student's score is 45% − 36% = 9% of the maximum marks, which equals 18 marks. So maximum marks = 18 ÷ 0.09 = 200."], ["Reasoning Ability", "If BAG is coded as 14 (the product of the positions of its letters in the alphabet), what is the code for DEAF?", ["16", "96", "120", "150"], 2, "B, A, G are 2, 1, 7 and 2 × 1 × 7 = 14. For DEAF, the positions are 4, 5, 1, 6, so the product is 4 × 5 × 1 × 6 = 120. The sum, 16, is a trap."], ["Numerical Ability", "What approximate value should come in place of the question mark (?)\n24.98 × 12.03 + 299.97 ÷ 6.02 = ?", ["340", "360", "330", "350"], 3, "Round each number: 25 × 12 = 300 and 300 ÷ 6 = 50. The total is about 300 + 50 = 350. Division is done before addition, as BODMAS requires."], ["Reasoning Ability", "Five friends A, B, C, D and E sit in a row facing north.\n• B sits second from the left end.\n• Only one person sits between B and D.\n• E sits immediately to the right of D.\n• A does not sit at either end.\nWho sits at the extreme left end?", ["A", "C", "E", "B"], 1, "B is 2nd, so D is 4th (there is no position 0). E is immediately right of D, so 5th. A cannot be at an end, so A is 3rd and C takes the left end: C B A D E."], ["Reasoning Ability", "Mohan walks 15 m towards north, turns right and walks 8 m, then turns right again and walks 9 m. How far is he from his starting point?", ["10 m", "14 m", "12 m", "8 m"], 0, "North 15 m, then right (east) 8 m, then right again (south) 9 m. He is 15 − 9 = 6 m north and 8 m east of the start. Distance = √(6² + 8²) = 10 m."], ["Reasoning Ability", "Statements: Some cups are plates. Some plates are spoons.\nConclusions: I. Some cups are spoons. II. No cup is a spoon.", ["Only conclusion I follows", "Only conclusion II follows", "Either I or II follows", "Neither I nor II follows"], 2, "Neither conclusion is certain on its own. But I and II form a complementary pair about the same two terms: one of them must always be true. Hence either I or II follows."]]};
